  "continuity": "All 139 tests (122 domain and 17 provider/cursor/mapping tests) and quality checks pass on 8446 unchanged inputs. Ten new files and two shared protocol files differ from accepted room-message worker inputs. No schema, DI or public group history dispatch changes.",
  "evidence": [
    "Distinct group owner/port validates exact original participants, Matrix users/devices, room and creator. Completed LEGACY metadata must be supplied by later current admission; the protocol itself grants no access.",
    "Group encryption purpose binds seven original owner/room coordinates. Group/company/account/device/room/server replay is rejected. Only exact original LEGACY room/device coordinates allow one old company cursor attempt after INVALID; missing keys and cancellation do not fallback.",
    "Shared company/group reader compares private positions before randomized encryption. Empty stalled pages terminate, nonempty stalled pages fail, advancing empty pages remain pageable. Cursor opening precedes provider I/O.",
    "Both adapters retain strict room/sender/event/state framing, original encrypted content and own transaction IDs while dropping unsafe fields. Context validates exact target and combined limit; single-event reads validate exact event identity.",
    "Actual Synapse tests cover original SPACE and LEGACY rooms through provider restart, finite pagination with no duplicate event IDs, original ciphertext/session/device/sender and creator, context and event reads. The LEGACY test starts with an actual old company page and continues its cursor under the group protocol.",
    "Existing company cursor/mapping tests and actual provider history pagination pass with the shared reader and unchanged company cursor purpose. No replacement SDK store or raw provider cursor is introduced."
  ],
